# This file was the Dynamics 365 Business Central (AL) template chosen when the
# repository was created. There is no AL code here and never will be, so it
# ignored nothing and hid nothing — replaced with the stack this project
# actually uses: Python on the server, React on the client.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# The built SPA is produced by `npm run build` on deploy, never committed — a
# checked-in bundle drifts from its source silently.
server/spa/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch
*.local

# Recorded narration.
#
# The real recordings now exist — 31 files, 51 minutes, 48MB — and they ARE the
# deployment artefact rather than a build output. They belong in the
# repository, and they are still excluded here because 48MB of binary in plain
# git is a decision to take on purpose: Git LFS is the way to take it, and it
# has not been set up yet.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS UNTIL THEN. A fresh clone has no narration and every slide
# falls back to the browser voice. `python -m tools.import_narration --check`
# reports it and exits non-zero. Relax this rule once LFS is in place.
assets/narration/*
!assets/narration/README.md
